============= CLI >>atomdb --help<< =============
usage: ncrystal_atomdb [options] [PATTERN ...]

Browse NCrystal's database of isotopes and natural elements, with their masses,
scattering lengths, and cross sections.

Each PATTERN can be:

  - an element (e.g. He, also selecting its isotopes),
  - an isotope (e.g. B10, with D and T meaning H2 and H3),
  - a condition, such as "absxs>1000" or A==0 (see --cond-help).

other options:
  -h, --help   show this help message and exit
  --cond-help  Show the properties usable in conditions and exit.
  --json       Output all properties of the selected entries as JSON.
  --ncmat      Output in NCMAT @ATOMDB format.

examples:
  ncrystal_atomdb He B10                  # natural He and its isotopes, and B10
  ncrystal_atomdb "absxs>1000"            # strong absorbers
  ncrystal_atomdb Gd --ncmat              # output in NCMAT @ATOMDB format

Use --cond-help for the list of properties.

============= CLI >>atomdb --cond-help<< =============
conditions:
  Conditions compare a property with a value, like "absxs>100" (conditions with
  < or > need quotes). Text comparisons ignore case.

examples:
  "absxs>1000"                  strong absorbers
  A=0 "cohsl<0"                 natural elements with negative cohsl
  He A!=0                       only the isotopes of He

properties:
  Z        atomic number
  A        mass number (0 for natural elements)
  mass     atomic mass [amu]
  cohsl    coherent scattering length [fm]
  cohxs    coherent scattering cross section [barn]
  incohxs  incoherent scattering cross section [barn]
  scatxs   scattering cross section [barn]
  absxs    absorption cross section at 2200m/s [barn]
